==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that distinct AccessAttempts must hold distinct AuditEntries. The injected violation forces two different AccessAttempts to share the same AuditEntry, simulating an in-place mutation (an 'updated' audit record). Both AppendOnly and FR_010_AuditImmutability assert that no two attempts share an entry, so they find a counterexample immediately.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutability, FR_012_RetentionFloor
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_RetentionFloor: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that Permitted outcomes require an active CareTeamMembership. The injected violation forces a Permitted RecordsLookup attempt to exist for a caller who has no active membership for the target patient, directly violating the care-team-only authorisation rule from FR-006.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamMembershipGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamMembershipGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ResponseShapeMapping  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_ResponseShapeMapping.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the outcome-to-response-shape mapping. The injected violation forces a Denied attempt to return OkShape, making the externally visible response distinguish 'denied' from 'not-found' and leaking the existence of the patient. Both NoInformationLeakage and FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenied catch this.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenied, FR_014_FR_015_ClinicalSafetyFields
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenied: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_FR_015_ClinicalSafetyFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the guarantee that every RecordsLookup attempt produces exactly one audit entry. The injected violation forces a RecordsLookup attempt to exist with no linked AuditEntry, simulating the 'record observed without audit trail' scenario that FR-013 and SC-002 prohibit.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_013_NoRecordWithoutAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_NoRecordWithoutAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CallerOperationConstraint  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CallerOperationConstraint.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the enforcement that callers may only invoke operations in their allowed permission matrix cell. The injected violation places an AuditOfficer on a RecordsLookup attempt, which is explicitly denied in the permission matrix and would allow an IG officer to read clinical records directly — violating LeastPrivilege.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_011_AuditSearchIGOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_AuditSearchIGOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that an audit entry's recorded clinician and snapshot role must match the AccessAttempt's actual caller. The injected violation forces an audit entry to name a different clinician than the one who made the request — a misattribution that would make the audit log forensically unreliable and violate FR-009's snapshot semantics.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_002_RoleFromIdentityContext, FR_009_AuditEntryFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_RoleFromIdentityContext: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditEntryFields: FAIL (expected)

